multi-horizon projections.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Create and optimize rations from ingredients, calculating nutrition and cost.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Generate pen-level daily feed plans based on bunk rates, ration, and animal counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Log feeding activity, calculate variances and costs, decrement inventory, and roll up lot consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Record lot weight measurements as a time series.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate and update feed-to-gain metrics and projected ship dates from feeding and weight data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide dashboards and reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a feed-to-gain report with lot comparisons, filters, and CSV or PDF export.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Create sample/mock data and a yard-level summary dashboard.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Deliver the proposed solution, architecture, app demo, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the feed-to-gain report and its exports follow the same yard and profitability access rules as dashboards?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Restrict report results and exports to the user's authorized yards and apply the same profitability restrictions as dashboards.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users sign in to access operational records and role-based permissions?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use email and password sign-in for the web app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may import source records and change PO-to-lot and lot-to-pen mappings?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only users with operational access can import source records and change mappings; other users can view them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may change target weights and growth-rate assumptions used for forecasts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized managers can change the assumptions; other users can view forecasts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may maintain inventory items, record receipts or adjustments, and change the wastage setting?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized inventory users may make these changes; operational users may view inventory and record feeding subject to stock controls.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may create, revise, optimize, and approve ration definitions?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only users with authorized ration-management access may perform these actions; other users may view rations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should feed-plan creation or adjustment permissions differ from updating a plan's execution status?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized planners generate or adjust plans; operators may update execution status for their assigned pens.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may add weight measurements to a lot's history?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only authorized livestock or operations users may add measurements; other users may view them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 22 requirements be approved as one run, or should some requirements be cut?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 22 requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the app handle a feeding save that times out when it cannot reliably tell whether the event was saved?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Remove the uncertain-save reconciliation requirement; show a timed-out save as unknown and leave retry resolution to the existing service/user workflow.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Should dashboard and yard-summary aggregates be guaranteed to exclude sample records, even when the service returns aggregates mixed with operational data?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Display the returned aggregate values as provided, without a sample-free guarantee.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build a responsive feedlot web app with email-and-password sign-in, permission-based navigation and actions, and clearing of protected data when a session expires or a protected request returns HTTP 401.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide authorized users with mock procurement and receiving import, PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen allocation with quantities and traceability, and display repeat-import matches and allocation conflicts without presenting matches as new records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Display animal and lot forecasts based on incoming data and yard defaults or lot overrides, show forecasts as unavailable without a positive gain rate, and restrict forecast-assumption editing to authorized managers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Display feed inventory and stock movements, allow authorized inventory users to maintain items, receipts, adjustments, and wastage settings, and show inventory projections for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons using saved feed plans and configured wastage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Present known actual wastage separately from delivered-feed consumption, and display inventory and projection empty states when returned data has no items or plans.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized ration managers create, revise, optimize, and approve rations; display ingredients, proportions, nutrition, and cost; and present the lowest-cost qualifying optimized mix without saving it until explicitly chosen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized planners generate or adjust dated pen-level feed plans from bunk rates, ration assignments, and animal counts, and display returned plan details, execution status, and review flags when relevant inputs change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Keep saved plans unchanged until an authorized planner confirms or regenerates a flagged plan, allow assigned-pen operators to update execution status, show service refusals, and display intake variance without automatically rewriting plans.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Let operational users record feeding activity by pen and lot, including lot allocations, and display returned variance, cost, energy, inventory consumption, status, and lot consumption and cost totals.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Display insufficient-stock errors without saving feeding events, provide permission-controlled correction and void actions, and show timed-out saves as unknown while retaining submitted event fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized livestock or operations users add lot weight measurements and display time-ordered measurement history with returned gain information.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Display returned lot performance metrics for days on feed, weight gain, average daily gain, feed consumed, feed conversion, cost of gain, and projected ship date, and refresh metrics after feeding or weight records change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Present explainable rule-based feeding or sale-timing suggestions based on lot weight-gain trends, leaving plan or sale changes to an authorized planner's explicit action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Display yard and lot performance, inventory, feeding, weight, cost, and energy on a dashboard, and let users choose the measure used to rank best- and worst-performing lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Provide filterable operational reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability that answer the specified pen, lot, ration, plan-variance, inventory, and cost-of-gain questions, with CSV export of filtered results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Restrict dashboard, report, and export data to records and profitability fields permitted for the signed-in user's authorized yards and permissions, removing data from view and later exports when permissions change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a feed-to-gain report comparing lot ADG, FCR, and cost of gain with date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters, and permission-controlled CSV or PDF exports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a filterable on-screen lot profitability list for authorized yards and CSV export of filtered authorized results, hiding profitability values when the user cannot view them.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized users load visibly designated sample data, prevent duplicate loads, require confirmation before reset or replacement, and distinguish sample from operational records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Exclude sample records from operational report and inventory-total views and exports, while displaying dashboard and yard-summary aggregate values as returned by the service.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Display a yard-level summary of active-lot total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost using returned aggregates, with unavailable values where required data is missing.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a delivery overview or presentation page with the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure every page works at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal page scrolling or overflow, and provide touch controls at narrow widths with a minimum target size of 44 by 44 CSS pixels.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}